      "classification": "recommended / primary",
      "rationale": "The fitted database covers ordinary low-temperature VLE/azeotrope behavior and excess enthalpy through 383 K, while the 423 K Barr-David isotherm provides a clean independent elevated-pressure check below ethanol's critical temperature. NRTL-PR gives 2.54% pressure AARD and y MAE 0.00997 at 423 K."
    },
