        350.0
      ],
      "P_bar": [
        0.1,
        190.0
      ],
      "classification": "validated engineering extrapolation with caveats",
      "rationale": "Across the 57-point high-T/P benchmark, NRTL-PR remains quite accurate (3.89% pressure AARD, y MAE 0.0108), while reconstructed UMR/UNIQUAC is substantially better (1.72% pressure AARD, y MAE 0.00457).",
      "caveats": [
        "Plain gamma-phi NRTL-PR or UNIQUAC-PR is not a rigorous standard-state treatment above ethanol Tc (~514 K); its success there is empirical.",
        "For work materially above ethanol Tc, prefer UMR/UNIQUAC or another EoS/GE formulation.",
        "Composition coverage narrows sharply with temperature: the validated two-phase branch is water-rich at the highest temperatures.",
        "At 623 K the 57-point benchmark contains only x_ethanol <= 0.052; do not interpret the 623 K result as full-composition validation.",
        "The Q_water=1.4 correction is inferred from reproduction quality rather than explicitly acknowledged in the 2011 paper."
      ]
    },
    "suggested_simulator_policy": [
      "Use NRTL-PR as the simple/default implementation over the primary range.",
      "Allow NRTL-PR through the useful engineering range with an extrapolation warning above ethanol Tc.",
      "If UMR/EoS-GE is available, switch to or prefer UMR/UNIQUAC for genuinely high-T/P ethanol-water work.",
